# Erase the Alnasl hall box back to new, without a screen.
#
# To use it: make a file called "alnasl-reset.txt" in this folder whose FIRST
# line is the word RESET (capitals, nothing else on that line), and boot the Pi.
# This example does not count as it is: its first line is this comment.
#
# At boot the box deletes the file first (so it cannot happen twice), then
# erases Alnasl's data, the settings, the Wi-Fi networks and the logs, showing
# its progress on the screen, and restarts into the first-time setup wizard.
# The system and Alnasl itself stay. Anything else on the first line: the file
# is deleted and nothing is erased.
